{"title":"2005 iTest Problems/Problem 35","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_35&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> satisfy the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/8/af8e30fd45d5f4d5baf0ef3492216bf134a4df89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x^2 - 9x + 19)^{x^2 + 16x + 60 }= 1?$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"227\" height=\"24\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_35&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This equation is satisfied when:\n</p><p>(1) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/7/1d743d82ae96a0d0f95214566023a4a8c473734f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2} + 16x + 60 = 0  \\Rightarrow  (x + 6)(x + 10) = 0  \\Rightarrow  x = -6, -10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"453\" height=\"21\" />;\n</p><p>(2) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/b/16b79b35e3e63448716045f650b9383af3bb14ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2} - 9x + 19 = 1  \\Rightarrow  x^{2} - 9x + 18 = 0  \\Rightarrow  (x - 3)(x - 6) = 0  \\Rightarrow  x = 3, 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"559\" height=\"21\" />;\n</p><p>(3) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/9/399bd765be25a3af4a668fb8a9d63406f9216737.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2} - 9x + 19 = -1  \\Rightarrow  x^{2} - 9x + 20 = 0  \\Rightarrow  (x - 4)(x - 5) = 0  \\Rightarrow  x = 4, 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"573\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>of which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/3/c43970aa97091f384854d477a1e1e07356887266.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> is eliminated from (3) since the exponent <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/7/09741227c20885fd71c6778d77daa3e427a1aaa7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{2} + 16(5) + 60 = 165$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"174\" height=\"21\" /> is odd and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/7/b474323fc4a716b99ebe8e70d72c09051ccdfa47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-1)^{165} = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"107\" height=\"21\" /> (a contradiction). Hence, the solution set is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/3/c7373a3367a2593731bb3491dff652948a04294c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\{-10, -6, 3, 4\\} \\cup \\{6\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"200\" height=\"20\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/1/a11484bbde19c74b5ead27e1c0c62b5d149fbb58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"21\" height=\"24\" /> values.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_35&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest\" title=\"2005 iTest\">2005 iTest</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems\